  "_framedNote": "A `framed` entry is traced to fill the common 100x100 viewBox, so its class scale is NOT in the artwork and the renderer applies `size` when drawing. An entry without it is a placeholder whose artwork already carries its scale - the Krelath placeholder heights run 38.6/47.8/55.2/64.4/75.4/92 for corvette through battleship, which is the size ladder itself - and scaling those again would apply it twice.",
  "_weaponRegionNote": "TURRET PLACEMENT, deferred until every fleet is traced (Chris, 2026-09-08). The point of recording this now: turret positions can be READ OUT OF THE ARTWORK rather than hand-authored. Glyph colours are semantic (data/ship-markup.json, art branch) and the marks are mirror-symmetric about the keel at distinct stations. Rulings below are Chris's, measured against the traced glyphs on this branch. EARTH - the painted orange cap, #e8792a. One per mount, and the count equals the authored mount count exactly: 1, 3, 5, 8, 13 for frigate, destroyer, light cruiser, heavy cruiser, battleship. VRAYGON - green, #3fd45c. Exact the same way: 1, 3, 6, 8, 13. Its markup names the region glow_green, by colour rather than by role. KRELATH - two different marks, which is why a single colour never matched. A BEAM is a yellow dome, #ffd90f, one per mount. A TORPEDO LAUNCHER is a squashed bronze hexagonal prism carrying THREE red hexagons, #e02a22, as warning markings on its top face, so red divides by three rather than counting one-to-one; the same red marks the airstrips on the carrier's elevators. Orange #f07820 is emissive glow and NOT a weapon marker - do not extract from it. KRELATH POINT DEFENCE - a hull that carries point defence shows ONE EXTRA dome, smaller than the battery domes, and it is not a battery mount. It is the unique smallest in its class: 2.2 against 3.7 on the frigate, 2.3 against 3.7 on the destroyer, 2.4 against 3.3/3.4 on the light cruiser. Heavy cruiser and battleship have pointDefence 0 in hullClasses and show no odd-one-out, as expected. Spans are only comparable WITHIN a class - the glyphs are traced to a common frame, so a small hull's fittings are larger in viewBox units. OPEN, settle before extraction starts: Krelath heavy hulls show fewer domes than they have beams - 4 against 5 on the heavy cruiser, 6 against 8 on the battleship - where the light hulls are exact. Occlusion from directly above is the likely cause but it is not confirmed. And the v3 brief already flags the Star Knight's red triplet resolving as one blob, so Krelath extraction must group marks into rings and hexagons before counting, never count raw paths. SOURCE FIXES, on the art branch: the Krelath region is misnamed nav_red in data/ship-markup.json, carried over from Earth where red really is a running light, and the v3 brief calls Krelath red 'a painted marking' two lines after saying its red hexagons mark torpedoes. Zandrax is not traced yet, so its weapon marking is unknown."
}